# @rt-category Test Scenes
# bdpt-room-furnace.pbrt -- a closed diffuse sphere lit by a point light at its centre: an interreflection furnace with a closed-form answer at every depth.
#
# Every wall point sees the light along its own normal at distance R = 1, so the direct irradiance is I everywhere, and a sphere's inside sees only
# itself, so the indirect irradiance is the wall's own radiosity B: B = rho (I + B). With I = pi and rho = 0.5 the radiance (B / pi, the same at every
# point) after d bounces is 0.5 * (1 + 0.5 + ... + 0.5^(d-1)): 0.5, 0.75, 0.875, ... -> 1.0.
# The camera sits inside, looking at the wall, so it sees neither the light nor the sphere's outside.

LookAt  0.5 0 0    1.5 0 0    0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 40 ]

Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 32 ] "integer yresolution" [ 32 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

LightSource "point" "rgb I" [ 3.14159265 3.14159265 3.14159265 ] "point3 from" [ 0 0 0 ]

Material "diffuse" "rgb reflectance" [ 0.5 0.5 0.5 ]
Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 1 ]
